{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And to his father he sent like this.</b> As this gift-offering — just as he gave provisions to his brothers for the way, so he sent to his father for the way. And what did he send? Ten donkeys and ten she-donkeys, to carry his load. And he sent this gift-offering as males and females, like the gift-offering that his father sent to Esau (Genesis 32): ״עזים מאתים ותישים עשרים״ — two hundred she-goats and twenty he-goats." "<b>בר and bread and food.</b> <b>בר</b> is grain, and it includes the five species. And <b>לחם</b> (bread) — these are types of legumes, such as beans and lentils, from which bread is made. And <b>מזון</b> (food) — these are types of fruits that serve as food for a person, such as figs and raisins and dates and the like. And know that every בר can be made into לחם, but not every לחם is from בר; and likewise every לחם is מזון, but not every מזון is לחם."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:30.742487348Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}